OriginLore (
    origin_id: "vacuum_adapted",
    canonical_name: "Vacuum Adapted",
    physical_description: "Heavily modified post-human variant optimized for sustained vacuum operation. Body presents as gaunt, tall (often above 2.0 meters), with thickened skin, reinforced bone structure, and an integrated secondary respiration system that can store approximately fifteen minutes of oxygen reserve. The eyes are protected by a permanent thin transparent membrane; the lungs have been modified to handle pressure cycling without rupture; the cardiovascular system runs at lower baseline pressure with sustained surge capacity. Average blood volume is approximately five thousand milliliters; clot rate is slightly higher than baseline human.",
    cultural_traits: "The vacuum-adapted population is small and concentrated almost entirely in the Belt and the Lagrange station belt. The original program was a Coalition military project of the 2191-2215 era, designed to produce a heavy-EVA infantry capable of sustained operations without standard vacuum suits. The program produced approximately seven hundred and forty modified individuals; the program was discontinued in 2215 after the Concordat's ethics committee determined that the modifications were too aggressive for voluntary military service to be a sufficient legitimating framework. The seven hundred and forty surviving modified individuals retain full Concordat citizenship and have, over the following thirty years, formed a distinct cultural community across the Belt. Vacuum-adapted culture is markedly stoic and centered on the practice of extended solo extra-vehicular activity; their funeral tradition involves the body's release into open vacuum with a controlled de-orbiting burn that brings it eventually into the sun.",
    gameplay_strengths: "Substantial vacuum exposure resistance (TTD approximately 4x baseline human). Substantial cold tolerance. Strong pressure-cycling resistance. Reduced respiratory afflictions (modified lungs). Integrated emergency O2 reserve (15 min in unprotected vacuum). Substantial G-force resistance (reinforced cardiovascular).",
    gameplay_weaknesses: "Limited compatibility with standard medical equipment (modified anatomy requires specialized intervention). Reduced caloric storage (modified metabolism is power-prioritized). Lower stamina ceiling than baseline human (less efficient at sustained exertion). Reduced cosmetic appearance options (heavy modification visible). Limited social compatibility (cultural distinctness).",
    home_world: "No fixed home; concentrated in Belt asteroid settlements (Ceres Concourse residential ring, Pallas Hold workshops, and approximately thirty smaller Belt habitats).",
    notable_origins_in_corefall_universe: [
        "Major Thane Larsen (Coalition, retired heavy-EVA infantry)",
        "Multiple Frontier crew members in Belt operations are vacuum-adapted",
        "Anders Karlsson (Belt prospector, original discoverer of asteroid 47-Family-1; vacuum-adapted)",
    ],
)
